-- Cosmix theme (strict-data .conf.mix) — copy to one of:
--   <cosmix config dir>/theme.conf.mix      (desktop-wide: every cosmix app)
--   <app config dir>/theme.conf.mix         (per-app override of the above)
--
-- The shared Cosmix config dir resolves as: COSMIX_ETC when set; otherwise
-- $COSMIX/etc when the running binary locates a checkout; otherwise the XDG
-- Cosmix config directory for an unrooted user install.
--
-- Resolution cascade: built-in Ocean-light  ←  shared  ←  per-app.
-- Missing files clear their layer. Palette validation and design authority
-- commit together: a malformed or mid-save layer is logged once and retains
-- both last-good values. A present-but-invalid design keeps the last-known-good
-- button table; it never silently falls through. Symlinked configured paths
-- are re-resolved on every reload.
--
-- The palette model is shared verbatim with the web design system
-- (dcs.spa / webd site.css): a scheme is a hue; only the accent's L/C is
-- materially per-scheme. See
-- _decisions/2026-07-22-cosmix-visual-identity-own-palette.md (in cmctl).

-- Pick a scheme + mode (the common case — matches the web setScheme/setTheme).
-- scheme: ocean | crimson | stone | forest | sunset | mono
-- mode:   light | dark
scheme: "ocean"
mode: "dark"

-- Optional per-token #rrggbb hex overrides, applied ON TOP of the scheme.
-- Uncomment to tweak individual console tokens; unset tokens keep the scheme.
-- These colours hot-swap for legacy UiTheme-token consumers. CtkButton does
-- not read these token overrides: its colours and metrics come from the
-- compiled design source described below.
--
-- surface:        "#0b0d17"   -- window background
-- panel:          "#141726"   -- strip panel
-- master_panel:   "#1a1829"   -- master strip panel
-- track:          "#070812"   -- fader/meter well
-- control:        "#2a2d45"   -- resting control body
-- control_active: "#8b8fe6"   -- fader fill / lit accent
-- thumb:          "#aab0f0"   -- fader/scrubber thumb
-- meter_green:    "#22c55e"   -- meter healthy   (status; scheme-invariant)
-- meter_amber:    "#f59e0b"   -- meter hot
-- meter_red:      "#ef4444"   -- meter clip
-- text:           "#e6e8f0"   -- primary text
-- text_dim:       "#8b90a6"   -- captions / readouts / footers

-- Legacy non-button layout metrics (pixels). Uncomment to override; relaunch
-- to apply. CtkButton metrics do not come from these fields.
-- control_gap:    8.0
-- corner_radius:  5.0
-- fader_width:    42.0
-- fader_height:   250.0
-- knob_size:      58.0
-- meter_width:    28.0

-- CtkButton design source contract
-- --------------------------------
-- This same theme.conf.mix may contain one COMPLETE `design` section copied
-- from ctk's shipped revision-1 source. CTK selects one whole source:
--
--   per-app design  <-  shared design  <-  embedded revision-1 design
--
-- Omitting `design` (as this selection-only example does) contributes no
-- design source. A partial or invalid section is rejected and the running app
-- keeps its last-known-good buttons; CTK never merges partial design overlays.
-- Saves are watched live, including atomic replacements. Byte-identical saves
-- are no-ops. The complete reference document is:
--   crates/cosmix-design/src/defaults/revision-1.theme.conf.mix
